<article class="env-definition" id="0DBL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DBL">Definition <span data-tag="0DBL">34.8.11</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathit{Sch}_{ph}$ be a big ph site containing $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>big ph site of $S$</em>, denoted $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{ph}$, is the site $\mathit{Sch}_{ph}/S$ introduced in Sites, Section <a href="/tag/00XZ" data-tag="00XZ">7.25</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>big affine ph site of $S$</em>, denoted $(\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph}$, is the full subcategory of $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{ph}$ whose objects are affine $U/S$. A covering of $(\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph}$ is any finite covering $\{ U_ i \to U\} $ of $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{ph}$ with $U_ i$ and $U$ affine. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>